<div class="wrap">

  <div class="hero">
    <p class="kicker">Hericium erinaceus</p>
    <h1>Lion's Mane</h1>
    <p class="lede">A shaggy, white, pom-pom-shaped mushroom made of cascading spines instead of gills — one of the most recognizable and sought-after mushrooms in cultivation.</p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>Lion's Mane grows as a single rounded mass of long, icicle-like spines that hang downward, giving it a shaggy, white, fur-like appearance that's easy to spot and hard to mistake for anything else. Unlike most mushrooms, it has no cap or stem in the usual sense — the whole fruiting body is one clump of tissue covered in spines.</p>
    <p>It belongs to a group called "tooth fungi," named for those spines, which take the place of gills or pores. In the wild, it grows on the wounds of living hardwood trees or on recently dead logs and stumps — beech, oak, and maple are common hosts. It behaves as both a saprotroph, feeding on dead wood, and a weak parasite, colonizing injured living trees through cracks or wounds in the bark.</p>
    <div class="facts">
      <div class="fact"><div class="label">Family</div><div class="value">Hericiaceae</div></div>
      <div class="fact"><div class="label">Habitat</div><div class="value">Hardwood wounds &amp; logs</div></div>
      <div class="fact"><div class="label">Feeding type</div><div class="value">Saprotroph / weak parasite</div></div>
      <div class="fact"><div class="label">Growth style</div><div class="value">Single spined mass</div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The life cycle</h2>
    <div class="cycle-diagram">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 600 600" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
        <circle cx="300" cy="300" r="220" fill="none" stroke="#24312280" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="4 8"/>
        <g font-family="Inter, sans-serif" font-size="15" fill="#e7ede6">
          <circle cx="300" cy="80" r="34" fill="#101710" stroke="#5fd068" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="300" y="86" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Spore</text>
          <circle cx="490" cy="220" r="34" fill="#101710" stroke="#5fd068" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="490" y="216" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Germin-</text>
          <text x="490" y="234" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">ation</text>
          <circle cx="420" cy="440" r="34" fill="#101710" stroke="#5fd068" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="420" y="436" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Myce-</text>
          <text x="420" y="454" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">lium</text>
          <circle cx="180" cy="440" r="34" fill="#101710" stroke="#ece4d3" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="180" y="436" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600" fill="#0a0f0a">Primor-</text>
          <text x="180" y="454" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600" fill="#0a0f0a">dium</text>
          <circle cx="110" cy="220" r="34" fill="#101710" stroke="#ece4d3" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="110" y="216" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Fruiting</text>
          <text x="110" y="234" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">Body</text>
          <circle cx="300" cy="300" r="40" fill="#101710" stroke="#8a6644" stroke-width="2"/>
          <text x="300" y="296" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600" font-size="14">Sporula-</text>
          <text x="300" y="313" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600" font-size="14">tion</text>
        </g>
        <g stroke="#5fd06880" stroke-width="2" fill="none" marker-end="url(#arrow)">
          <path d="M 328 92 A 220 220 0 0 1 468 198"/>
          <path d="M 470 250 A 220 220 0 0 1 442 412"/>
          <path d="M 392 458 A 220 220 0 0 1 208 458"/>
          <path d="M 158 412 A 220 220 0 0 1 130 250"/>
          <path d="M 132 198 A 220 220 0 0 1 272 92"/>
        </g>
        <defs>
          <marker id="arrow" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" refX="4" refY="4" orient="auto">
